  "rationale": "Resubmission of the thrice-accepted Pareto-optimal stream (4096 DMA input bytes, 46 commands). B contributes exactly 10 distinct 16x16 tiles (2 k-chunks x 5 n-blocks), each loaded once = 2560 bytes. A has only 2 distinct tiles, but the 32-row scratchpad fits just two 16-row tiles: a B tile always occupies one slot and an A tile the other. With only 2 accumulator tiles (32 rows), at most two k=0 partial sums are live, so one A0 load serves at most 2 chunk-0 computes before A1 must be loaded for their chunk-1 accumulates; hence ceil(5/2)=3 loads each of A0 and A1 = 6 A tiles = 1536 bytes. Total 16 mvins x 256 = 4096 bytes, provably minimal. Command count 46 is minimal: 10 computes (2 per n-block for K=32) each require one preload (10), 5 mvouts cover the 16x80 C, 16 mvins, 4 configs, 1 fence. Loop p over N//32 pairs blocks a=2p, b=2p+1: c0a (A0*B0a overwrite acc rows 0-15), c0b (A0*B0b overwrite acc rows 16-31), then A1 loaded, c1a/c1b (accumulate), then both accumulator tiles drained via mvout to C offsets 32p and 32p+16 (store stride 320 bytes = 80 int32). Per-block K order (chunk 0 overwrite, chunk 1 accumulate) satisfies the ordered-reduction contract. Block 4 is handled flat after the loop with reloaded A0/A1 and B tiles at offsets 64 and 1344. All scratchpad/accumulator starts are multiples of 16 within the 32-row capacities; every compute is immediately preceded by its own preload with accumulated=false and bd_spad_addr=4294967295; accumulate-mode computes and all mvouts follow initialized accumulator contents."
